From: TactiQ OS BSP <bsp@tactiqedge.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3588s-rock-5a: expose the TPM event log

U-Boot measures the boot and extends PCR 0 and 1, but the kernel only
publishes /sys/kernel/security/tpm0/binary_bios_measurements if it can
find the event log area itself. Without it a PCR value is a number with
no way to check what produced it, which is exactly what the measurement
is supposed to make verifiable.

drivers/char/tpm/eventlog/of.c:tpm_read_log_of() looks for linux,sml-base
and linux,sml-size on the TPM node first; when neither is present it
falls back to tpm_read_log_memory_region(), which takes the first
memory-region phandle of that node. The phandle form is used here so the
bootloader and the kernel name the same area the same way: U-Boot reads
it through the identical mechanism (lib/tpm-v2.c), and the address stays
in one place instead of being repeated as two magic numbers.

The area is the one the bootloader writes: 0x18100000, 64 KiB, sitting
directly above the ramoops reservation added in the previous patch and
inside the same verified gap. The bootloader-side reservation lives in
the U-Boot device tree, which the kernel never parses, so this node is
required rather than duplicated.

no-map is set, unlike ramoops. The kernel reaches this area through
devm_memremap in tpm_read_log_memory_region, which does not need the
linear map; ramoops needs it because pstore goes through memremap on a
mapped region. The two nodes differ here on purpose.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ BSP integration - board-specific
 memory reservation; not intended for mainline submission]
Signed-off-by: TactiQ OS BSP <bsp@tactiqedge.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-rock-5a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-rock-5a.dts
index 8fa6286..5383961 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-rock-5a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-rock-5a.dts
@@ -869,6 +869,7 @@
 		reg = <0>;
 		/* Conservative initial bus clock; raise after bring-up. */
 		spi-max-frequency = <1000000>;
+		memory-region = <&tpm_event_log>;
 	};
 };
 
@@ -884,5 +885,11 @@
 			console-size = <0x00040000>;
 			record-size = <0x00020000>;
 		};
+
+		tpm_event_log: tpm-event-log@18100000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x18100000 0x0 0x00010000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 	};
 };
